{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/4943-wasteland-disquite-managing","id":4943,"title":"Wasteland/Disquite managing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T04:01:28-08:00","id":4943,"title":"Wasteland/Disquite managing","content":"I was reading the Promothean book, and while I'd really, really like to run a game someday, I was wondering: it looks to me like between the Wasteland and the Disquiet rules, any game that goes for more than a few weeks in-game would have to involve moving, which suggests a nomadic kind of story. Which is fine, the journey is half of Promethean.<br /> <br /> But I was wondering, is that as big an issue in-play as it seems to me? Like, if I'm running a game which I plan on going for say six in-game months, should I tell the players &quot;this game will involve moving from place to place, so plan for it&quot;, or doesn't it really come up as long as the players keep an eye on X?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T05:01:23-08:00","id":4964,"title":"","content":"Promethean is designed to be nomadic, both as a deliberate subversion of the &quot;city-level&quot; play that is assumed for nWoD, and to reinforce the tragic mood. You have no home, nowhere to call your own. You'll never have a place that you belong in, but you'll keep searching anyway.<br /> <br /> If you want advice for a nomadic game, check out World of Darkness: Midnight Roads. It's a guide to nomadic games and my personal favorite blue book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:25:56-08:00","id":5020,"title":"","content":"\u201cThe Lonely Man\u201d (the theme music from the old <i>Incredible Hulk</i> TV series) is appropriate mood music for a <b>Promethean</b> session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:48:50-08:00","id":5229,"title":"","content":"In the Merits section of the core book you'll find special notes explaining why it's hard for Prometheans to get certain Merits. Their location Merit, Lair, is also specifically designed to have a cheaper XP cost for their size due to players likely having to leave them during a chronicle. You can run a chronicle in phases, with each phase being a different city or area. That adds the race against time element that should be present as the players try to get what they need done before Wasteland and Disquiet &quot;catch&quot; them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:13:15-08:00","id":5353,"title":"","content":"...or you can make the game less nomadic, or nomadic within a city/county, by tweaking Wasteland. Either map it to Azoth (Azoth 1 Prometheans taint rooms, Azoth 10 entire cities) or Pyros use.(the more is used in area the more the Wasteland spreads). It doesn't weaken Promethean too much to do this, IMO, as they'll still have to move (or stay in a very corrupted lair - the sewers, perhaps?). I like to keep Disquiet nasty, though. Being a Promethean has to be suck or why become human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:03:22-08:00","id":7202,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Allan53;n4943But I was wondering, is that as big an issue in-play as it seems to me? Like, if I'm running a game which I plan on going for say six in-game months, should I tell the players &quot;this game will involve moving from place to place, so plan for it&quot;, or doesn't it really come up as long as the players keep an eye on X?[/QUOTE]<br /> Make sure your players know that their characters are cursed, and that staying too long in one place, or interacting too much with the same social network can have devastating effects. <br /> <br /> But on the other hand, don't let Disquiet or the Wasteland derail the story you're trying to tell. My personal take on Disquiet and Wasteland is to pace them so they serve the story, ignoring the dice rolls (keep them up to keep your players on their toes, though!) and advancing DQ/WL when doing so raises the stakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T14:12:39-08:00","id":9172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/4943-wasteland-disquite-managing?p=7202#post7202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the other hand, don't let Disquiet or the Wasteland derail the story you're trying to tell. My personal take on Disquiet and Wasteland is to pace them so they serve the story, ignoring the dice rolls (keep them up to keep your players on their toes, though!) and advancing DQ/WL when doing so raises the stakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking I'd run Wasteland more narratively, rather than using the (frankly confusing) system presented in the book. Disquiet, where I've been butting up against is, how do I run that so that it's believable? I mean, I get Disquiet isn't rational and such forth, but speaking as an ST it seems it'd be hard to show in the NPCs without just making everyone act like tools all the time, which'd mean the whole social side is pointless for the players/characters to engage with?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or you can make the game less nomadic, or nomadic within a city/county, by tweaking Wasteland. Either map it to Azoth (Azoth 1 Prometheans taint rooms, Azoth 10 entire cities) or Pyros use.(the more is used in area the more the Wasteland spreads). It doesn't weaken Promethean too much to do this, IMO, as they'll still have to move (or stay in a very corrupted lair - the sewers, perhaps?).</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I like. Keeps Wasteland to be a problem (which it totally should be), but not the sheer level of &quot;yep, need to move on every week or so unless I want to screw over everyone within a mile of that truck stop I had lunch at&quot; which it seems to be as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T17:33:04-08:00","id":9340,"title":"","content":"An interesting house rule I read online was that the ST moved the Wasteland effect to awake Pandorans to make Prometheans less villainous, but people can still mistake it for the Promethean's fault (since it Pandorans are only awake around Prometheans). Disquiet will still be a problem though, so while the characters might be able to stay in one place, people will still hate them and they'll attract Wasteland-creating Pandorans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1021-raneth","name":"Raneth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T23:15:35-08:00","id":21463,"title":"","content":"TBH, after the current Scion game ends, I plan on running a Promethean game. I had plans to keep them moving from place to place as they go along their own Pilgrimage until, as they get close to the end of it, that they settle onto one city. The reason why is that I want them to set in some roots so that, after they Redeem, they can pick up as Hunters. I had planned on providing some ST Fiat Homebrew as to why the Wastelands (not necessarily the Disquiet) was lessened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}